<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Lead My Company Privacy Policy, covering AI communications, appointments, SMS consent, and personal data.">
  <section class="document">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Lead My Company</strong><br />Effective date: November 17, 2026<br />Last updated: November 17, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>Lead My Company ("LMC", "we", "our", or "us") is an AI-powered business communication and automation platform operated by BONSES INOVA SIMPLES (I.S.), registered in Brazil under CNPJ 68.814.207/0001-33. We are committed to protecting your privacy and handling personal information responsibly.</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, protect, share, and process personal information when you visit our website, use our platform, interact with our AI assistants, or receive communications through our services.</p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on your interactions with our services, we may collect:</p>
    <h3>Personal and Contact Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Names and contact details.</li><li>Email addresses and telephone numbers.</li><li>Business names and professional information.</li><li>Account credentials and communication preferences.</li></ul>
    <h3>Appointment and Communication Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Appointment dates, times, and scheduling preferences.</li><li>SMS messages and communication history.</li><li>Call recordings and transcriptions, where legally permitted.</li><li>Customer inquiries and AI-assisted interactions.</li><li>Appointment confirmations and rescheduling requests.</li></ul>
    <h3>Technical Information</h3>
    <ul><li>IP addresses and device information.</li><li>Browser type and operating system.</li><li>Website usage and diagnostic information.</li><li>Security logs and authentication events.</li></ul>
    <h3>SMS Consent Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Whether a customer has agreed to receive SMS notifications.</li><li>Date, time, and method of consent.</li><li>Messaging preferences.</li><li>Opt-out requests and consent changes.</li></ul>
    <p>We may receive this information directly from users, from authorized businesses using our platform, or through their interactions with our services.</p>

    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We process personal information to provide and maintain services; manage appointments and communications; send authorized transactional SMS notifications; operate AI-powered customer service systems; respond to inquiries; secure our platform; prevent fraud; improve reliability and performance; and comply with legal obligations. We do not treat consent to receive transactional SMS notifications as authorization to send unrelated marketing messages.</p>

    <h2>4. SMS Messaging Privacy</h2>
    <p>Lead My Company supports transactional SMS communications, including appointment confirmations, reminders, scheduling changes, rescheduling instructions, and requested verification codes.</p>
    <h3>4.1 Consent</h3>
    <p>SMS notifications require appropriate consent from the recipient. Consent may be collected through an authorized booking process, verbal agreement, or another clearly disclosed opt-in mechanism. Providing a telephone number alone does not constitute consent. Consent to receive SMS notifications is optional and is not a condition of purchasing goods or services.</p>
    <h3>4.2 Message Frequency and Charges</h3>
    <p>Message frequency varies according to appointment activity and customer requests. Message and data rates may apply.</p>
    <h3>4.3 Opting Out</h3>
    <p>You may withdraw your SMS consent at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong>. For assistance, reply <strong>HELP</strong>. Opt-out requests are processed according to applicable requirements, and appropriate suppression records may be maintained to prevent unauthorized future communications.</p>
    <h3>4.4 Protection of SMS Consent Data</h3>
    <p>We do not sell, rent, or share mobile phone numbers, SMS opt-in information, or messaging consent with third parties or affiliates for their own marketing or promotional purposes. All other categories of information sharing described in this Privacy Policy exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent.</p>
    <p>Service providers may process information strictly as necessary to deliver authorized messages and operate the messaging service, subject to appropriate contractual and confidentiality safeguards. SMS consent is specific to the business and messaging program for which it was obtained. It is not transferred to unrelated businesses for their independent use.</p>

    <h2>5. AI-Powered Communications</h2>
    <p>Our platform uses artificial intelligence to assist with customer inquiries, scheduling, and business communications. AI interactions may involve processing messages, appointment details, and relevant conversational context. Where required by law, customers will be informed when interacting with an automated assistant. Call recordings and transcriptions are collected only when permitted by applicable law and after any required notice or consent. We do not authorize businesses to use our services for unlawful surveillance or unauthorized recording.</p>

    <h2>6. Sharing and Disclosure of Information</h2>
    <p>Personal information may be disclosed to service providers when reasonably necessary to operate our services, including cloud hosting and infrastructure providers; telecommunications and messaging providers; authorized calendar and business integrations; payment processors; and security and technical support providers.</p>
    <p>Information may also be disclosed when required by applicable law or valid legal process. Businesses using Lead My Company may access information relating to their own customers according to their authorized use of the platform. We do not sell personal information to data brokers or disclose customer information to unrelated advertisers for their own marketing purposes. SMS opt-in information and consent remain subject to Section 4.4.</p>

    <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational safeguards designed to protect personal information. These may include encryption in transit, authentication and access controls, role-based permissions, security monitoring and logging, and restricted access to customer information. No internet-based service can guarantee absolute security. If a security incident affecting personal information occurs, we will investigate and provide notifications when required by applicable law.</p>

    <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to provide services, fulfill contractual obligations, maintain security, resolve disputes, and comply with applicable laws. Retention periods may vary depending on the type of information, including communication records, call recordings, transcriptions, appointment information, and account data. When personal information is no longer required, it may be deleted or anonymized, except where continued retention is legally required or otherwise permitted. SMS opt-out records may be retained as necessary to respect withdrawal of consent.</p>

    <h2>9. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>Lead My Company operates from Brazil and may use service providers located in the United States or other jurisdictions. Personal information may be processed outside a user's country of residence. Where required, we apply appropriate safeguards for international transfers under applicable data protection laws, including Brazil's Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados (LGPD).</p>

    <h2>10. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have the right to request access to your information; correct inaccuracies; request deletion of eligible information; withdraw consent where processing relies on consent; object to certain processing activities; request information about data use; and exercise other available privacy rights.</p>
    <p>To submit a privacy request, contact joao@leadmycompany.com. If your information was collected by a business using our platform, that business may be responsible for handling your request. We will provide appropriate assistance where required.</p>

    <h2>11. Cookies and Website Technologies</h2>
    <p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies for authentication, security, preferences, and essential website functionality. Where optional analytics or other non-essential technologies are used, we will provide applicable disclosures and consent choices as required by law. You may manage certain cookies through your browser settings.</p>

    <h2>12. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Our platform is intended primarily for businesses and their authorized users. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children for unauthorized purposes. If we become aware that personal information has been collected unlawfully, we will take appropriate steps to address the situation.</p>

    <h2>13. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Our services may integrate with external platforms, including calendar providers, telecommunications networks, AI service providers, and payment processors. These providers may maintain their own privacy policies and legal obligations. We encourage users to review applicable third-party privacy policies when using those services.</p>

    <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our services, technology, legal obligations, or data-processing practices. The most recent version will be published at https://leadmycompany.com/privacy/. Material changes will be communicated when required by applicable law.</p>

